WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.340
in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen."

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:13.220
The reading from the Sinhaxadion for June 26 on which we commemorate our righteous

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:23.200
Father David of Thessalonica, this earthly angel and heavenly man renounced his earthly land

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:30.640
of Mesopotamia and all worldly attachment at an early age to take up his cross and follow

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:38.000
the Lord by becoming a monk in the monastery of St. Theodore and Mercurios, generally known

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:47.040
as of the Cucullates in Thessalonica. He mortified the desire of the flesh by a sustained

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:55.280
askecies and was guided in the science of virtue by meditating on Holy Scripture and the lives

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:02.640
of the saints. The holy stylites, Simeon, the elder, Simeon of the wonderful mountain,

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:12.320
Daniel, Potapius, and those like them enjoyed his special admiration and, burning with desire

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:20.640
to imitate them, he climbed up into an almond tree to the right of the church and settled on one of

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:30.320
its branches as a new kind of stylite, dendrite, offering himself as a spectacle to both angels

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:38.880
and men he patiently endured all the rigors of the climate battered by the wind, burned by the sun,

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:47.200
drenched by the rain and exposed to cold and snow during the winter. He was even deprived of the

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:54.560
stability that the stylites enjoyed on their columns and perched on his branch was like a bird

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:02.480
that continually lifted up its voice night and day to God in the sweetest melodies of his prayers

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:11.920
and ceaseless thanks-givings. Devout men full of zeal for virtue became his disciples

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:17.120
and begged him to come down from his perch to become their guide in the monastic life.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:26.640
David replied that he would only do so after three years if he received a sign from God to so do.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.880
When three years had passed an angel appeared to him and made it clear that he had pleased God by

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:42.960
his manner of heavenly life but that it was now time to descend and to retire to a cell before

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:51.840
being given another mission. David made this message known to his disciples, who, after having prepared

00:02:51.840 --> 00:03:01.040
a new dwelling for him, a tiny space, made him get down from his branch. This he did in the presence

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:06.960
of Metropolitan Dorothils of Thessalonica and a large number of clerics.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:15.040
The divine liturgy was celebrated after which the saint entered into reclusion to the accompaniment

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:22.640
of a spiritual concert of hymns and thanks-givings. Praying continually without distraction,

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:30.160
the saint acquired extraordinary grace and fervor from God. One night, the soldiers who were

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:35.280
keeping guard on the ramparts of the city saw that fire was streaming from his cell.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:42.080
As soon as morning came, they rushed to the cell but found to their amazement,

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:48.720
but it was completely undamaged and the man of God was safe and sound.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:56.960
The same miracle happened again and again and the whole population became witnesses of it.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:05.120
One of the city's inhabitants, Paladios by name, having seen this miracle occur several times,

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:14.480
said to himself, if God accords such glory to His servants on earth, what must be the glory reserved

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:25.200
for them in the age to come when their faces will shine like the sun? He left to become a monk in Egypt.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:33.520
From this glory of God, which was the object of His contemplation, Saint David received the

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:40.000
power to drive out demons. He also gave sight to the blind and healed all manner of sicknesses

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:49.280
invoking the name of Christ and, in this way, being regarded by the whole town as its guardian angel.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:57.680
At that time, the combined forces of the Slavs and Avar hordes, who had already ravaged almost the

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:07.040
whole of Macedonia, were threatening Cermium, where the prefect Elyricum was living. He wrote to

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:15.280
Aristides, Metropolitan of Thessalonica, asking him to send a virtuous man as an ambassador to Emperor

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:22.560
Justinian, to ask him for permission to transfer his residence to Thessalonica, where the ramparts of

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:30.400
the city protected it from all the assaults of the barbarians. The clerics and important officials,

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:37.120
whom the bishop gathered together, all cried with one voice, that only David the recluse was able

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:45.040
of representing them before the Emperor. The saint refused at first citing his advanced age,

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:53.200
but remembering the message of the angel, he afterwards submitted, prophesying that he would die

00:05:53.200 --> 00:06:01.280
a short distance from his cell on his return. When Saint David came out of his cell, all the people

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:08.000
prostrated themselves on seeing his imposing figure. His hair and beard reached his feet,

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:13.680
and his face was like that of patriarch Abraham, shining with glory.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:22.080
He set out for Byzantium with two disciples, but the Emperor was away when he reached the palace,

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:29.200
and he was received by Empress Theodora, who asked him to pray for the salvation of the Empire,

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:37.840
and of the city. On his return Emperor Justinian, learning that a man of God was present at the court,

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:46.960
called together the senate, so that it might hear his request. St David picked up live coals

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:55.680
in his hands, and placing incense on them, sensed the Emperor and all the senate for about an hour,

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:04.320
without being at all harmed. The Emperor was greatly impressed, and exceeded to the request

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:11.360
of the Metropolitan which David had presented, that the seat of the prefect of Elicrium be transferred

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:21.360
to Thessalonica, that transfer happened in 535. He then sent David home, showing him great marks of

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:28.400
honor. When the ship came near the lighthouse of Thessalonica, once the saint's monastery could

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:36.960
be seen, David told his disciples that his hour had come, and after giving them the kiss of peace,

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:46.160
and uttering a last prayer, he gave his blessed soul into God's hands, in about the year 540.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:54.160
Despite a strong wind, the ship came to a halt, and the smell of incense filled the air,

00:07:54.160 --> 00:08:01.200
while heavenly voices were heard. When they ceased, the ship continued its journey.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:08.240
The Metropolitan and all the people were there on the shore to welcome the saint, and he was buried

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:15.040
in his monastery in accordance with his last request. A hundred and fifty years later,

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:22.400
the abbot, wishing to steal part of his relics for himself, had the tomb opened, but the stone which

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:30.240
covered the body, broke it into a thousand pieces. Thirty years later, the next abbot succeeded in

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:38.880
opening the tomb and found the saint's body in corrupt. For centuries, these precious relics

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:47.120
continued to work miracles. Through the prayers of our holy fathers, O Lord Jesus Christ our God,

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:55.760
of mercy on us, and save us.
